{
 "name": "harp_seal_costume_prone",
 "description": "Doug's homemade HARP SEAL suit worn lying flat (057), built like seal_costume_prone so it slots onto the on_back rig: pale silver #d9dcdf felt pillow-soft body, a big black felt horseshoe/harp saddle patch sewn on the back with white running stitches, a black felt face-mask hood band round his head (whisker pads + whiskers), dark front flipper, paired tail flippers past his feet. Reads clearly different from 051's grey speckled seal_costume_prone. Place it AFTER Doug at x = Doug x + 30*scale, same y and scale, rotate -90 (stored pre-rotated). Covers about 540x170 on screen at scale 1 (Doug-frame x -314..306, y -98..72; whisker tips reach x -346). Head, face and red cap stay visible.",
